{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-05T11:51:59.773Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"543a385e8166d7855a7e72c0","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-glossary-yrza"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"SDK gap: protected extension envelopes need native cost and producer cursor controls"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Release blocker for the exact native output-control contract. Published SDK CommandDefinition.read_output only opts read-only handlers into host shaping; validateReadOutputOptions runs before parser overrides and refuses mutation cost flags. Native output cursors are decoded and applied outside the handler, so producer-owned pagination is applied twice. No public consume-cursor or mutation-envelope capability exists in ExtensionCommandSdk. Public declarations and open upstream searches were checked; no matching open issue was found. Upstream issue creation is outside this task. The package uses explicit budget and cursor fallback flags without shadowing native flags or misdeclaring writes as reads."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["release-blocker","sdk-gap","upstream:pm-cli"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-05T11:51:59.773Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-05T11:51:59.773Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Upstream provides truthful mutation cost controls and producer-owned native cursor 